WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:15.000
Platform teams often repeat application setup and discover identity,
networking, and operational decisions late.

00:15.000 --> 00:30.000
This foundation offers a consistent local starting point:
typed APIs, reusable UI, database tooling, and specification-led changes.

00:30.000 --> 00:45.000
This is a real local browser capture, not a customer application.
There is no live AI agent or deployed Azure environment.

00:45.000 --> 01:00.000
We select light theme on the existing neutral homepage.
Shared primitives use semantic design tokens.

01:00.000 --> 01:15.000
Keyboard navigation is part of presenter review.
Automated accessibility checks do not replace assistive-technology testing.

01:15.000 --> 01:30.000
We select dark theme. The content and scope remain unchanged.
No product navigation, roles, permissions, or application data are defined.

01:30.000 --> 01:45.000
The reusable value is the foundation and its explicit boundaries,
not an invented business workflow.

01:45.000 --> 02:05.000
The liveness route returns status live.
This proves process responsiveness, not database connectivity.

02:05.000 --> 02:25.000
Readiness returns status ready. This capture runs with
DATABASE_MODE=local-password and local PostgreSQL enabled.

02:25.000 --> 02:45.000
The versioned health API returns status ok and apiVersion v1.
It exercises the contract pipeline, not a product transaction.

02:45.000 --> 03:05.000
The implemented local diagram shows the browser crossing
the HTTP boundary into Next.js and its in-process packages.

03:05.000 --> 03:30.000
Local PostgreSQL is loopback-bound with no product tables.
Database-disabled readiness would not establish database connectivity.

03:30.000 --> 03:50.000
The Azure diagram is a scaffolded-disabled TARGET, not deployment evidence.
Dashed paths do not represent active controls.

03:50.000 --> 04:15.000
Identity, networking, residency, monitoring, and recovery decisions remain open.
Foundry is false-only; application trace export is disabled.

04:15.000 --> 04:35.000
Bring one application request and your platform/security owners.
The workshop produces an adoption decision and scoped implementation backlog.

04:35.000 --> 04:50.000
A pilot needs a governed PRD and measurable acceptance criteria.
Any Azure operation requires separate, explicit authorization.

04:50.000 --> 05:00.000
This gives your team a consistent starting point and exposes
decisions still required before deployment. Readiness gates remain open.
